OL,3,GNEWSAAlleyway crime fears fail to stop
OL,4,Ahomes plan
OL,5,
OL,6,FApproval has been given for 87 homes to
OL,7,Fbe built despite a councillor claiming
OL,8,Fresidents will be "terrorised" by crime
OL,9,Fif a new alleyway is opened alongside
OL,10,Fit.
OL,12,FRedcar and Cleveland Borough Council
OL,13,Fsupported the plans submitted by
OL,14,FGleeson Regeneration for the
OL,15,Fdevelopment on farmland in Brotton,
OL,16,Fwhich would include new pedestrian
OL,17,Faccess to Landsdowne Road.
OL,19,FLocal councillor Barry Hunt said: "It
OL,20,Fwill be used by bikes and for
OL,21,Fanti-social behaviour, delivering
OL,22,Fdrugs. People will be terrorised."
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
